1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Bc4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. Re1 d5 7. Bxd5 Qxd5 8.
Nc3 Qa5 9. Nxe4 Be6 10. Bd2 Bb4 11. Nxd4 Nxd4 12. c3 O-O-O 13. cxb4 Qf5 14. Rc1
Bd5 15. Ng3 ({Both BCM and University Chess give} 15. Ng5 {here but this must
be wrong.}) 15... Qg6 16. Rxc7+ ({Both BCM and University Chess give 16 Rxc7+
and I'm inclined to believe them. CHESS, Vol.34/573-4, February 1969, p169,
doesn't have the full score, but shows a position after} 16. Bf4 Ne6 {-
diagram in CHESS - and continues with} 17. Rxe6 $1 Qxe6 18. Rxc7+ Kb8 19. Re7+
Ka8 20. Rxe6 {stating that "the material plus soon triumphed". Had that been
the move order, Black would probably have found 16...Bc6! when White has
nothing special. However, the full score given in the next issue gives 16
Rxc7+.}) 16... Kb8 ({Stockfish 16:} 16... Kxc7 $5 17. Bf4+ Kc8 18. Qxd4 b6 19.
b5 $14) 17. Bf4 Ne6 18. Rxe6 Qxe6 (18... Bxe6 19. Rd7+ Kc8 20. Qd6 $18) 19.
Re7+ Ka8 20. Rxe6 Bxe6 21. Qa4 a6 22. h3 Rd5 23. Be3 Bd7 24. Qb3 Be6 25. Qc3
Rg8 26. Qc7 Rc8 27. Qb6 Kb8 28. Ne4 Rb5 29. Qd6+ Ka8 30. Qd4 Kb8 31. Nd6 {
Sources: BCM, February 1969, p48; University Chess 1968/69 (BUCA bulletin), Ed.
Hartston/Keene; CHESS, Vol.34/573-4, February 1969, p169 (erroneous position
and some moves); CHESS, Vol.34/575-6, March 1969, p197} 1-0

